{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795637651,"nonce":"5GQtKSLT85om8QICByLDcbIgKKM=","title":"Component pages: browser shortcuts fire over a live demo that is editing","message":"Reported by use: in the browser, Ctrl+F in the code editor opened the browser's find.\n\nThe component pages and the example pages run demos in a worker (web/components/runtime/host.js). The host forwards keydown to the worker and the worker's answer, whether a handler prevented the default, arrives too late to cancel the event. The host cancelled only navigation keys and keys that make text, so Cmd and Ctrl shortcuts reached the browser. The main-thread web runner already cancels Cmd or Ctrl with a letter before it dispatches.\n\nFix: while the worker reports an editable focus, the host cancels Cmd or Ctrl with a letter, and F3. Copy, cut and paste are left to the clipboard events. Not checked in a real browser.","files":null}]}